{
  "email": "james.oconnor@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Ticket sender reports the orders@ shared mailbox disappeared from Outlook folder list. Checking account, devices, and mailbox status per KB-011 steps."
}

{
  "hostname": "BL-DT-0108",
  "reason": "Checking whether the user's desktop is online and has no warnings, as part of diagnosing the missing orders@ shared mailbox in Outlook."
}

{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi James, thanks for reporting this. Your mailbox account itself looks healthy, so the orders@ mailbox is most likely just not being re-added to Outlook on your computer. Could you try these steps? 1) Make sure your desktop (BL-DT-0108) is turned on and connected to the network. Our records show it offline, so it may need a restart. 2) Once it's on, fully close and reopen Outlook. The shared mailbox is usually added automatically after a restart. 3) If it still doesn't show, open Outlook on the web (outlook.office.com) and check whether orders@ appears there under Add shared folder or mailbox. Then reply and let us know what you see, and whether you were recently told that access to orders@ was granted. If it still doesn't appear after these steps, we'll follow up with a closer check of the access permissions. Also note that if you need to send as orders@, that requires a separate Send As permission, which adding the mailbox alone doesn't give you.",
  "internal_note": "Sender James O'Connor (user_id 8, Operations, usual hours 06:00-14:00 America/Chicago). Account active, not blocked, no failed logins, mailbox 29.7% used (not a quota issue). Device BL-DT-0108 is offline, last check-in 2026-10-11 01:36 UTC, no disk or device warnings. Did not run KB-011 steps with the user yet: asked user to power on/restart the PC, restart Outlook, and check OWA for orders@. I have no tool to verify whether the orders@ 'Full Access' grant exists; if the user was never granted access, per KB-011 it needs mailbox owner approval then Tier 2 for the change (see KB-006). Next: if OWA also lacks orders@, confirm the grant with the mailbox owner and escalate to Tier 2 if access was never granted. Offline status may simply reflect after-hours shutdown, so it is not yet conclusive.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-011",
    "KB-009"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
